1
00:02:30,723 --> 00:02:34,895
<v AGENT> Good afternoon and welcome to Habitat Hunters. You must be Joseph.

2
00:02:34,895 --> 00:02:40,617
<v RENTER> Yes, that’s right. You said on the phone that I could come by at 2:00. Sorry, I’m a little early.

3
00:02:40,617 --> 00:02:46,445
<v AGENT> No problem at all. In Calgary’s market, you have to move fast if you want a good apartment!

4
00:02:46,445 --> 00:02:54,281
<v RENTER> Actually, I’d settle for almost anything. I’ve been here ten days and the hotel is ruining me. My father has me on a strict budget.

5
00:02:54,281 --> 00:03:02,456
<v AGENT> Sit right down here now, sir. Let’s talk a little about the places before we go have a look. Now, we have four apartments available.

6
00:03:02,456 --> 00:03:06,261
<v RENTER> OK, could you tell me more about those four apartments?

7
00:03:06,261 --> 00:03:16,867
<v AGENT> Sure. The first one is on Beatle Road, just a block off-campus. It’s a 3-bedroom with a bathroom and a living room and a great Italian restaurant right next to it.

8
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:17,844
<v RENTER> How much?

9
00:03:17,844 --> 00:03:23,536
<v AGENT> Well, it’s $435 a month, including Internet and utilities.

10
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:26,979
<v RENTER> Okay, that sounds reasonable. Any drawbacks to the house?

11
00:03:26,979 --> 00:03:34,529
<v AGENT> There’s a really big garden, but it hasn’t been taken care of over the years and is just too big to clean up nicely.

12
00:03:34,529 --> 00:03:37,820
<v RENTER> Hmm. That sounds okay. Tell me about the next option.

13
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:48,153
<v AGENT> The other 3-bedroom apartment is on Oakington Avenue on campus. It is right near the building where you have classes, and the kitchen and living room are
newly furnished.

14
00:03:48,153 --> 00:03:50,873
<v RENTER> Wow, that sounds like a pretty good option.

15
00:03:50,873 --> 00:04:01,643
<v AGENT> Well, it is a cool apartment, but since it’s a dormitory, the living room, bathroom, kitchen, and washing machine are all shared. It would be nice not to have to buy living room furniture, though.

16
00:04:01,643 --> 00:04:03,283
<v RENTER> And how much is this one?

17
00:04:03,283 --> 00:04:12,728
<v AGENT> $400 per month for a bedroom with an air conditioner. For a bedroom without an air conditioner, you would pay less, $340 for it.

18
00:04:12,728 --> 00:04:21,585
<v RENTER> Yikes, even with the air conditioner, it sounds really inconvenient to have to share facilities. I’ll never cook if I have to walk down the hall to use the kitchen.

19
00:04:21,585 --> 00:04:23,265
<v AGENT> Yeah, that’s true.

20
00:05:09,678 --> 00:05:13,319
<v AGENT> Anyway, the next place is a 2-bedroom on Mead Street.

21
00:05:13,319 --> 00:05:16,272
<v RENTER> Oh, I like Mead Street - that’s off campus, right?

22
00:05:16,272 --> 00:05:21,698
<v AGENT> Yep. It’s pretty cool, but it only has 2 bedrooms, plus a living room and a study.

23
00:05:21,698 --> 00:05:24,665
<v RENTER> But I want to live together with my two friends.

24
00:05:24,665 --> 00:05:29,373
<v AGENT> So you could make the study into a small bedroom if you end up living with them.

25
00:05:29,373 --> 00:05:34,981
<v RENTER> Also, we guys want a TV and DVD player since we’re all so much into movies.

26
00:05:34,981 --> 00:05:39,596
<v AGENT> Well, this place has a great TV and VCR, but no DVD player.

27
00:05:39,596 --> 00:05:44,029
<v RENTER> No DVD? That’s so weird. Are any other facilities provided?

28
00:05:44,029 --> 00:05:48,009
<v AGENT> As you said, weird enough, it also comes with a washbasin.

29
00:05:48,009 --> 00:05:53,021
<v RENTER> Is there a washing machine? I think we need that more than just a washbasin.

30
00:05:53,021 --> 00:05:55,895
<v AGENT> I'm afraid there’s no washing machine in the apartment.

31
00:05:55,895 --> 00:06:02,320
<v RENTER> Wow, that’s so old-fashioned! Maybe it’s not the best choice for three college guys. How much is it?

32
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:09,029
<v AGENT> Well, it’s $600 per month, but of course it would be cheaper if you made it into 3 bedrooms instead of 2.

33
00:06:09,029 --> 00:06:10,824
<v RENTER> Where is this apartment located?

34
00:06:10,824 --> 00:06:14,829
<v AGENT> It’s 2500 Mead Street, where there are a lot of bars.

35
00:06:14,829 --> 00:06:22,817
<v RENTER> It would be affordable, but it would get pretty noisy. And that sounds really expensive for an old place in a noisy area. How about the last place?

36
00:06:22,817 --> 00:06:30,020
<v AGENT> This one’s on-campus in the Devon Close complex. It’s a one-bedroom, so it will be a little quieter than the Mead Street place.

37
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:34,488
<v RENTER> One bedroom, huh? That could be good for focusing on my studies. What else does it have?

38
00:06:34,488 --> 00:06:50,604
<v AGENT> It comes with a living room and a study, and includes a really nice lamp in the study that has a bunch of different settings. You know what else is cool? There’s a dining hall downstairs so all evening meals are free. You can purchase breakfast and lunch, but meals after 6 p.m. are free.


39
00:06:50,604 --> 00:06:54,456
<v RENTER> Wow, this place sounds too good to be true. Is it really expensive?

40
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:58,163
<v AGENT> It’s alright - $500 per month, but there’s no bathroom.

41
00:06:58,163 --> 00:07:00,295
<v RENTER> What? No bathroom?

42
00:07:00,295 --> 00:07:04,453
<v AGENT> Well, there’s no bathroom in the apartment, but there’s one at the end of the hall.

43
00:07:04,453 --> 00:07:09,659
<v RENTER> Hmm. Thanks, I think now I just have to decide whether I want to live alone or not.

44
00:07:09,659 --> 00:07:11,404
<v AGENT> Yeah, which one do you prefer?

45
00:07:11,404 --> 00:07:14,922
<v RENTER> I think I’d choose either this apartment or the one on Beatle Road.

46
00:07:14,922 --> 00:07:19,938
<v AGENT> OK. You’d better think about it, and then you can contact me ASAP.

47
00:07:19,938 --> 00:07:21,530
<v RENTER> Fine, thanks for your help!

48
00:07:21,530 --> 00:07:22,648
<v AGENT> You’re welcome...